       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rebecca Sutton Koeser",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Throughout the REST API, the log message can be omitted (whether it was intended to be optional or not).  Ingest is the only action I know of where an audit trail event is not created when no log message is supplied (various modify actions work fine without a log message, and an audit trail is created for those modifications).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
